## Methodology & Sourcing Notes

### GWP Basis
The NL-4 Premium Schedule and NL-34 Geographical Distribution both report **Gross Direct Premium** on a single statutory basis (figures originally in ₹ Lakhs, converted ÷100 to crore). Care Health's IRDAI filings do not separately disclose an "ex-1/n" basis, so this GWP figure represents the sole available (statutory, 1/n-inclusive) basis — consistent with the instruction to prefer the statutory basis where a choice exists.

### Retail Health GWP
This is the Health segment's total Gross Direct Premium from the NL-4 Premium Schedule (₹6,609.78 cr). A separate retail-only sub-split excluding group health was not disclosed in the NL forms, so this figure represents the total Health segment GWP (Care's dominant business line).

### PAT
Sourced from the NL-2 Profit & Loss Account, "Profit/(Loss) After Tax," cumulative column for the period Upto the Quarter ended 31-Dec-2025 (₹47,974 lakh = ₹479.74 cr, IGAAP basis). No IND AS/IFRS-reconciled quarterly report was locatable for Care Health for this period, so the IFRS-basis PAT is not populated.

### Ratios (Claims, Expense, EoM, Commission, Combined)
Taken directly from the **NL-20 Analytical Ratios Schedule**, cumulative "Upto the Quarter ended 31st December 2025" column — these are the company's own disclosed ratios, not independently recomputed.

### Solvency Ratio
1.70x, taken directly from **NL-26 (Table IB)**, "Solvency Ratio (Total Available Solvency Margin / Total Required Solvency Margin)," as at 31-Dec-2025.

### Net Worth
Calculated as Share Capital (₹99,583 lakh) + Reserves & Surplus (₹1,59,140 lakh) = ₹2,58,723 lakh (₹2,587.23 cr), per the NL-8 and NL-10 schedules feeding into the NL-3 Balance Sheet "Shareholders' Funds" line.

### AUM
Calculated as Total Investments — Shareholders' (₹2,59,585 lakh) + Policyholders' (₹7,65,026 lakh) = ₹10,24,611 lakh (₹10,246.11 cr), per the NL-12/NL-12A Investment Schedules.

## Caveats

- No 9MFY26 investor-presentation deck exists for Care Health Insurance (unlisted entity); all figures are drawn exclusively from the statutory IRDAI NL public-disclosure PDF for Q3 FY26 (cumulative period ended 31-Dec-2025).
- IFRS-basis PAT and claims ratio, and retail health market share, are not disclosed anywhere in the available statutory filing and have therefore been left blank rather than estimated.
- All values reflect the company's own reported figures in the NL returns; no independent recalculation was performed beyond simple lakh-to-crore unit conversion and net-worth/AUM summation from disclosed balance-sheet/investment-schedule line items.</ans>
